{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.SimpleGraph.DegreeSum","lean:module:Mathlib.Logic.Relation","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.linearLayout_family_not_hasBulk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.linearLayout_family_not_hasBulk","kind":"theorem","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LinearLayoutNoBulk.lean#L279-L292","doc":"**No family of connected linear-layout graphs has a bulk.** Take one such graph `G A` on\n`Fin A` for every `A`; its surface count is `2` from `A = 2` on, so it neither diverges nor is\n`o(A)`. This is the scope-(b) closure of Avenue 2 over the framework's encoding: the invariant is\nlinear layout, and every word `atom_braid_word_3A` builds has it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.surface_eq_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.surface_eq_two","kind":"theorem","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LinearLayoutNoBulk.lean#L262-L277","doc":"**Surface count of a connected linear layout is `2`** for every `n ≥ 2`: the two ends of the\npath. Constant — the shape `CoordinationBulkCriterion.boundedSurface_not_hasBulk` rules out. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.surface","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.surface","kind":"def","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LinearLayoutNoBulk.lean#L259-L260","doc":"The **surface** of a graph: the number of vertices with fewer than two neighbours. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.card_edgeFinset_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.card_edgeFinset_eq","kind":"theorem","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LinearLayoutNoBulk.lean#L248-L257","doc":"**Bond count of a connected linear layout is `n − 1`** — affine in `n`, the `p = 1` law. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.card_filter_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.card_filter_lt","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LinearLayoutNoBulk.lean#L229-L246","doc":"`#{v : Fin n | v + 1 < n} = n − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.card_filter_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.card_filter_pos","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LinearLayoutNoBulk.lean#L210-L227","doc":"`#{v : Fin n | 0 < v} = n − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.degree_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.degree_eq","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LinearLayoutNoBulk.lean#L189-L208","doc":"The degree of `v` in a connected linear layout: one for each existing neighbour\n`v − 1`, `v + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.adj_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.adj_iff","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LinearLayoutNoBulk.lean#L180-L187","doc":"Adjacency in a connected linear layout is exactly consecutiveness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.chained_linearLayout_adj_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.chained_linearLayout_adj_succ","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LinearLayoutNoBulk.lean#L166-L177","doc":"A **connected** linear-layout graph contains every consecutive edge: it is the whole path. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.chain_le_of_missing_edge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.chain_le_of_missing_edge","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LinearLayoutNoBulk.lean#L148-L163","doc":"In a linear layout with the edge `{k, k+1}` absent, no chain of adjacencies from a vertex\n`≤ k` ever reaches a vertex `> k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.not_linearLayout_of_card_edge_gt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.not_linearLayout_of_card_edge_gt","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LinearLayoutNoBulk.lean#L143-L145","doc":"An edge set with more than `n` bonds is not a linear layout. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.card_edgeFinset_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.card_edgeFinset_le","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LinearLayoutNoBulk.lean#L132-L141","doc":"**Any linear layout has at most `n` edges** (degree sum `≤ 2n`). So an edge set with more\nthan `n` bonds — the max-contact / deltahedron count `3n − 6` for `n ≥ 4`, the complete graph's\n`n(n−1)/2` for `n ≥ 4`, the sub-affine true packing's `≈ 6n` — is not a linear-layout graph, and\nthe encoding cannot express it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.not_linearLayout_of_degree_ge_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.not_linearLayout_of_degree_ge_three","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LinearLayoutNoBulk.lean#L125-L130","doc":"A vertex of degree three or more is impossible in a linear layout: the max-contact packing\n(degree up to 12) and the complete graph (degree `n − 1`) are not linear-layout graphs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.degree_le_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.degree_le_two","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LinearLayoutNoBulk.lean#L108-L123","doc":"The neighbours of `v` in a linear layout lie in `{v−1, v+1}`, so there are at most two. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.card_filter_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.card_filter_succ","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LinearLayoutNoBulk.lean#L90-L106","doc":"The successor filter `{w | v + 1 = w}` has one element if `v + 1 < n`, none otherwise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.card_filter_pred","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.card_filter_pred","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LinearLayoutNoBulk.lean#L71-L88","doc":"The predecessor filter `{w | w + 1 = v}` has one element if `0 < v`, none otherwise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.Chained","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.Chained","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LinearLayoutNoBulk.lean#L64-L67","doc":"Every two vertices are joined by a chain of adjacencies (connectedness, spelled out as the\nreflexive-transitive closure of `G.Adj`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.LinearLayout","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk.LinearLayout","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LinearLayoutNoBulk.lean#L60-L62","doc":"A graph on `Fin n` is a *linear layout* if every edge joins consecutive vertices. ","signatureChunk":0}]}